@startuml hold-states
title Hold (L1 to L6, CR-04): a tentative claim on a venue period, with an expiry
' Hand-written from modules/venue/repo/holds.ts and holdExpiry.ts and modules/venue/domain/hold.ts;
' statuses in backend/packages/contracts/src/venueHolds.ts. The timers are the HoldExpiry workflow
' (planning-core/src/temporal/workflows/holdExpiry.ts).
hide empty description
skinparam shadowing false

state "Requested" as REQUESTED
state "Held" as HELD
state "Converted" as CONVERTED
state "Released" as RELEASED
state "Expired" as EXPIRED

[*] --> REQUESTED : coordinator asks for a hold (one live hold per event and venue)
REQUESTED --> HELD : Venue Staff place it, with an expiry (inserts a HELD slot)
REQUESTED --> RELEASED : released before it is placed
HELD --> CONVERTED : converted into a booking request's booking
HELD --> RELEASED : released (the slot is released)
HELD --> EXPIRED : the HoldExpiry timer fires at the expiry (the slot is Expired)
CONVERTED --> [*]
RELEASED --> [*]
EXPIRED --> [*]

note right of HELD
  A reminder goes out at the expiry minus the lead time.
  Venue Staff may move the expiry (PATCH /holds/{id}/expiry);
  the timers restart. The expiry is decided under the hold's
  row lock with the database clock, so an early or late timer is harmless.
end note
@enduml
